 "final_passage": "On the Kestrel-Grid test split, Eddyline achieved lower MAE than Brenna-ODE (0.212 vs 0.219) while using substantially fewer function evaluations (17.8 vs 64 NFE per window) and lower latency (112 ms vs 241 ms per batch of 256). Eddyline also outperformed the reference non-ODE forecaster Sluice-TCN in MAE (0.212 vs 0.231), but at higher latency (112 ms vs 38 ms per batch of 256). The efficiency advantage of Eddyline over Brenna-ODE was consistent across both NFE and latency, although the absolute MAE improvement was small (0.007).",
